1. To create a default user ---> useradd

2. How to create user with customization:
 
   -u    (Specific UID)
   -g    (Specific primary group)
   -G    (Secondary group)
   -s    (Assign no shell/ No login)

2. How to create group
   # groupadd <name_group>

3. How to make add and existing user in secondary group:  
   # usermod -aG  <group_name>  <User_name>

4. How to assign elevated privileges to a user:
   # visudo
   
   <user_name>  ALL=(ALL)  ALL    (With Password)

   <user_name>  ALL=(ALL)  NOPASSWD: ALL  (Without Password)

5. How to assign elevated privileges to a group:
   # visudo
   
   %<group_name>    ALL=(ALL)  ALL    (With Password)

   %<group_name>    ALL=(ALL)  NOPASSWD: ALL  (Without Password)

6. How to lock and unlock Users:

   # passwd -S <user_name>    (To get status of user passwd)
   # passwd -l <user_name>    (To lock the passwd of user)
   # passwd -u <user_name>    (To unlock the passwd of user)
   # grep bob  /etc/passwd    (To get status of user passwd)
   
   # usermod -L <user_name>    (To lock the passwd of user)
   # usermod -U <user_name>    (To unlock the passwd of user)
   # passwd -S <user_name>    (To get status of user passwd)
   # grep bob  /etc/passwd    (To get status of user passwd)

